{{also|Appendix:Variations of "bi"}}
==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|вꙑ-}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*vy-||out}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro}} {{m|ine-pro|*(H)ud}} (Derksen) or {{m|ine-pro|*ūd-}} : {{m|ine-pro|*ūt-}} ({{xlit|ru|Черных}}). In Slavic the final consonant was dropped.

Cognates include {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|out}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|aus||out}}.

===Prefix===
'''вы-''' (vy-) (this prefix almost invariably bears the stress in perfective verbs)

# {{cx|used with verbs|lang=ru}} [[out]], [[out from]] {{gloss|describing an action of moving outside from inside}}
#:* {{l|ru|идти́}} — ''to go''
#:* {{l|ru|выходить|вы́йти}} — ''to go out''
# {{context|used with verbs|lang=ru}} [[completion]] or [[fulfillment]]
#:* {{l|ru|кури́ть}} — ''to smoke''
#:* {{l|ru|выкуривать|вы́курить}} — ''to smoke to the end''

